dzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_5653.jpeg&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_5653.jpeg&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_5653.jpeg&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_5653.jpeg&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_5653.jpeg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w\" src=\"/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_5653.jpeg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75\"/></div></div><article class=\"prose-none space-y-4 font-body text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.85] text-ink\"><p>6 out of 108 Parshvanath - Shri Amijhra Parshvanath, Amjhera (Madhya Pradesh).</p><p>Mulnayak: White colored approximately 135 cm high idol of Lord Amijhara Parshvanath in Padmasana posture. There is a canopy of 9 snake hoods over the head of the idol.</p><p>Shrine: It is in the center of Amjhera village.</p><p>Historicity: The ancient name of Amijhara Tirtha was Kundanpur. This magnificent and miraculous idol was installed in Vikram Samvat year 1548 under the auspices of Acharya Vijaysurishwarji. Since a lot of nectar (ami) was coming out from the idol of Lord Parshvanath, hence this idol started calling it by the name of Shri Amizhara Parshvanath. When King Sandhya of this region came to Kundanpur village and was impressed by the miracles of this idol, the king named this village Amijhara.</p><p>Other Temples: There is no other temple. Not a single Jain family lives in this village and there is more Muslim population in the village, but there is a system of food hall and dharamshala.</p><p>Art and Sculpture: The Nine-Hawthorn Statue is artistic and beautiful. There are three salvats below the navel of this idol which you will not see or find in any other idol. The aura of the face of this idol of Shri Amizhara Parshvanath is of great faith and devotion, very miraculous, brilliant and shining. Devotees come and worship here with great faith and devotion.</p><p>Directions: The nearest railway station to Indore is at a distance of 88 kilometers. The nearest town is Dhar at a distance of 32 km and Mohankheda at a distance of 25 km and Bhopawar (Shri Shantinath Bhagwan) Tirtha and Navratna Sagar Samadhi Sthal are at a distance of 10 km. Bus services and private vehicles are available from here. Dharamshala and bhojanhala facilities are available here. There is also a sub-shelter here.</p><p>108 Shri Amizhara Parshvanath Shwetambar Jain Teerth, Bohra Bakhal, Amjhera, Madhya Pradesh 454441.</p><p>Trust: Shri Amijhara Parshvanath Shwetambar Jain Temple, Post: Amijhara - 454441, District: Dhar, State: Madhya Pradesh.</p><p>Praise of Lord Parshvanath:</p><p>I remained lost in the worldly wanderings and suffered a lot of pain.</p><p>I became tired, I became defeated, I came to seek refuge in you.</p><p>Reaching you, I bow my head and pray to you.</p><p>Come, the world has given up, let me confess my love to you.</p></article><nav class=\"mt-14 flex items-center justify-between border-t border-sandstone-deep/60 pt-6\"><a class=\"group flex items-center gap-1.5 font-ui text-sm text-ink-soft hover:text-maroon transition-colors\" href=\"/en/tirtha/tirtha-006\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-left h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m15 18-6-6 6-6\"></path></svg><span class=\"max-w-[10rem] truncate sm:max-w-xs\">Sri Amijhara Parshvanath (Gandharya Parsh